---
/* Component — PageHeader
 * The page's top bar. Its regions are PageBrand, PageNav and PageActions,
 * each placing itself in an explicit grid column.
 *
 * A three-column `1fr auto 1fr` grid: the outer columns split the leftover
 * width evenly and the centre takes exactly its content, which is what centres
 * the middle region against the bar rather than against its siblings. Because
 * each region names its own column, the geometry holds for any subset — a
 * header carrying only a nav is still centred, and one carrying only actions
 * still sits at the far edge. Region order in the markup is therefore free.
 *
 * A full-width edge-to-edge band: as a direct child of Page (outside PageMain's
 * content tracks) it spans the whole window width on its own — no margins, no
 * bleed tricks — and the raised fill bleeds edge to edge with it. Flat and
 * cornerless, to read as chrome rather than a floating card. The inline padding
 * uses the same centred-column formula as PageMain's gutters: since padding
 * insets the *content* without shrinking the element's own box, the fill still
 * spans full width while the region content caps at --bravoixr-page-max and
 * lines up with the page column below. The fill themes with the page via the
 * semantic dark override. */
---

<header>
  <slot />
</header>

<style>
  header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    padding-block: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    padding-inline: max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2));
    background: var(--bravoixr-color-surface-raised);
  }
</style>
